    "bottomLine": "The best all-round mattress for most seniors: cushioned on top, supportive underneath, with a firm edge to sit on.",
    "description": "The DreamCloud Premier is our first choice for most older sleepers because it gets the basics right without asking you to pick between comfort and support. The 13-inch build puts a quilted CloudQuilt euro top and a contouring memory foam layer over an adaptive support foam and 8 inches of individually wrapped coils. DreamCloud lists it as medium-firm. In practice that means the top cushions shoulders and hips, which many people with stiff joints appreciate, while the coils keep you from sinking so deep that rolling over becomes work. The maker says the edge is reinforced with a higher-density foam frame, which helps when you sit on the side of the bed to put on socks or steady yourself before standing. At 13 inches it also lifts the sleeping surface a little higher than a thin bed-in-a-box, which can make getting up easier on a standard frame. The Amazon listing for the queen gives 700 coils. The trade-offs: the memory foam layer can sleep warm, and some independent reviewers have questioned how well it holds up over many years. The 365-night trial and Forever Warranty soften that risk. If you sleep hot, look at the Purple Restore; if you want to choose your own firmness, the Brooklyn Bedding Signature Hybrid."
  },
  {
    "id": "nectar-premier-hybrid",
    "name": "Nectar Premier Hybrid 13\" Mattress",
    "category": "13-inch Hybrid, Medium",
    "badge": "Best for Couples",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Memory foam and pocketed coils that many couples choose to limit motion transfer",
      "Reinforced perimeter coils keep the edge firm, per the maker",
      "Amazon also sells it bundled with a Nectar adjustable base",
      "Cooling cover with more cooling fibers than the Nectar Classic Hybrid, per Nectar",
      "365-night trial and Forever Warranty"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Memory foam feel can make changing position slower",
      "Amazon listings disagree on medium versus medium-firm",
      "Weight limits vary by size"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "The quiet bed for couples on different schedules, and the easiest route to an adjustable base on Amazon.",
    "description": "The Nectar Premier Hybrid is the mattress we would point couples to, especially when one partner gets up in the night and the other is a light sleeper. Nectar builds it in 13 inches: a cooling cover, 2 inches of memory foam, 2 inches of responsive support foam, 8 inches of individually wrapped coils and a 1-inch base foam. Memory foam absorbs movement, and the wrapped coils move on their own rather than as one unit, so a partner turning over or getting up is less likely to wake you. Owners commonly describe it as a quiet bed. The maker says the perimeter coils are reinforced, which keeps the sides usable for sitting. Nectar lists the feel as medium, though some Amazon listings call it medium-firm. It is also one of the easier mattresses to pair with an adjustable base, because Amazon sells it bundled with a Nectar adjustable base that offers head and foot incline. That takes the guesswork out of compatibility. The trade-off is that memory foam responds slowly. People who find it hard to roll over or sit up may prefer the bouncier feel of the Purple Restore or the euro top of the DreamCloud. The 365-night trial and Forever Warranty match DreamCloud, its sister brand."
  },
  {
    "id": "purple-restore-hybrid",
    "name": "Purple Restore Hybrid Mattress",
    "category": "11.5-inch GelFlex Grid Hybrid, Soft or Firm",
    "badge": "Best for Hot Sleepers",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "2-inch GelFlex Grid has open air channels that Purple says draw heat away",
      "Responsive surface makes rolling over and sitting up easier than slow memory foam",
