---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Bedroom & Sleep",
    tags: [
      "best mattress for seniors",
      "best mattress for elderly",
      "mattress for older adults",
      "mattress for seniors with back pain",
      "best mattress height for seniors",
      "adjustable base mattress"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Mattresses for Seniors</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          The right mattress for an older sleeper is easy to get in and out of, firm at the edge, kind to the joints and quiet enough to share. Here is how to choose one.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#dreamcloud-premier"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Jump to the Rankings
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Alex Rivers</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Home Improvement Editor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="8.9k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#getting-in-and-out" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. Getting In and Out of Bed</a>
          <a href="#firmness" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Firmness and Joint Comfort</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. The 6 Best, Ranked</a>
          <a href="#adjustable-base" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Adjustable-Base Compatibility</a>
          <a href="#temperature" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Temperature</a>
          <a href="#motion-isolation" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Motion Isolation for Couples</a>
          <a href="#mattress-types" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Hybrid, Foam or Innerspring</a>
          <a href="#delivery-and-trial" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Delivery and Trial</a>
          <a href="#when-to-replace" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. When to Replace</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          For older sleepers the best mattress is not just the most comfortable one. It sits at the right height, has a firm edge to sit and stand from, cushions sore joints without trapping you, and works with an adjustable base if you want one.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="getting-in-and-out" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Getting In and Out of Bed: Height and Edge Support Come First
          </h2>

          <p>
            Comfort gets most of the attention in mattress shopping, but for many older sleepers the moments that matter most are getting into bed and getting out of it. A bed that is too low, too soft at the edge or hard to roll over on turns every morning into an effort. Before you think about memory foam versus coils, think about height and edge support.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Total Bed Height</h3>

          <p>
            The useful measurement is the top of the mattress from the floor, which is frame height plus foundation plus mattress. A common guideline is that when you sit on the edge, your feet should rest flat on the floor with your knees at roughly a right angle, or slightly higher than your hips. For many adults that lands somewhere around 20 to 25 inches, but measure your own knee height rather than relying on a number. A 13-inch mattress on a standard frame sits higher than a 10-inch one; a thick pillow top higher still.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Edge Support</h3>

          <p>
            When you sit on the side of the bed to dress or steady yourself before standing, a soft edge sinks and tips you forward. A reinforced edge, made with firmer perimeter coils or a band of dense foam, gives you a stable surface to push off from. DreamCloud, Nectar and Brooklyn Bedding all describe reinforced or supportive edges on the models in this guide.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Ease of Movement</h3>

          <p>
            Slow memory foam holds the shape of your body, which feels cradling but can make rolling over or sitting up harder. Hybrids with responsive foam, latex or Purple's gel grid push back faster. If you already find it hard to change position, lean toward a more responsive surface.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Bed Rails and Handles</h3>

          <p>
            A bed assist rail that slides under the mattress can help some people get up safely, but check that it fits your mattress height and foundation. An occupational therapist can advise on the right setup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="firmness" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Firmness and Joint Comfort: Medium to Medium-Firm Suits Most
          </h2>

          <p>
            There is no single right firmness for older sleepers, but most people land somewhere between medium and medium-firm. That range gives enough cushion to ease pressure at the shoulders and hips while keeping the spine supported and the surface easy to move on.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Side Sleepers With Sore Shoulders or Hips</h3>

          <p>
            Side sleeping concentrates weight on the shoulder and hip. Many side sleepers with joint discomfort prefer a medium or softer bed, or a firmer bed with a cushioned top. Our guide to the <a href="/best-mattress-for-side-sleepers/">best mattress for side sleepers</a> goes into more detail.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Back Sleepers and Lower Back Discomfort</h3>

          <p>
            Back sleepers usually do best on medium-firm, which keeps the hips from sinking below the shoulders. Many people with lower back pain prefer this range, though a mattress is not a treatment. Talk to your doctor or physical therapist about persistent pain, and see our guide to the <a href="/best-mattress-for-back-pain/">best mattress for back pain</a>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">When Firmer Is Not Better</h3>

          <p>
            An old belief holds that a very firm mattress is best for the back. A bed that is too firm can create pressure points and does not let the body's curves settle, so many older sleepers find it uncomfortable. If a mattress is close but slightly too firm, a <a href="/best-mattress-topper/">mattress topper</a> can soften it.
          </p>

